= Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine - Prompt 02

#section_label("Prompt metadata")
- Title: Why Medicine
- Limit: 500 words
- Cycle used in this repo: 2025-2026 from Med School Insiders
- Source: https://medschoolinsiders.com/medical-school-secondary-prompts-database/loyola-university-secondary-essay-prompts/
- Local notes file: prompt-02.local.md

#section_label("Prompt text")
Considering all that you could do with your life, how have you discerned your decision to become a physician? What is particular to the practice of medicine and the vocation of a physician that draws you to apply to medical school versus another helping/caring profession? What experiences, conversations, and encounters have informed your decision to apply?

#section_label("Shared backbone files")
- typst/shared/future-goals.typ
- typst/shared/clinical.typ

#section_label("future-goals backbone")
= Future Goals Backbone

== Near-Term
What do you hope to learn or become in medical school?

== Longer-Term
What kind of physician or leader are you building toward?

== Continuity
Connect your future goals to real prior experiences.
#section_label("clinical backbone")
= Clinical Exposure Backbone

== Best Experience
Choose the single clinical experience that best changed your understanding of medicine.

== Learning
- What did you observe about patient care?
- What did you learn about physicians?
- What did you learn about yourself?

